{"name":"Swamp Thing","hex":"#162825","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"swamp","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An area of wet (water-saturated), spongy (soft) land, often with trees, generally a rich ecosystem for certain plants and animals but ill-suited for many agricultural purposes.","A place or situation that is foul or where progress is difficult."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To drench or fill with water.","To overwhelm; to make too busy, or overrun the capacity of."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swamp"},{"term":"thing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["That which is considered to exist as a separate entity, object, quality or concept.","A word, symbol, sign, or other referent that can be used to refer to any entity."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To express as a thing; to reify."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thing"}],"entries":[{"title":"Swamp Thing","blocks":[{"text":"Swamp Thing is a fictional character appearing in American comic books published by DC Comics. While several incarnations of the character have since debuted, the original was created by writer Len Wein and artist Bernie Wrightson and first appeared in House of Secrets #92. The character found perhaps its greatest popularity during the original 1970s Wein/Wrightson run and in the mid-late 1980s during a highly acclaimed run under Alan Moore, Stephen Bissette, and John Totleben."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/57/Swamp_Thing_%28Alec_Holland%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swamp_Thing"},{"title":"Swamp Thing (2019 TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Swamp Thing is an American superhero horror television series created by Gary Dauberman and Mark Verheiden for DC Universe, based on the DC Comics character of the same name. The series follows medical doctor Abby Arcane encountering the eponymous Swamp Thing, a plant-elemental creature who fights malevolent forces around a Louisiana swamp."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/65/Swamp_Thing_2019_TV_series.webp/330px-Swamp_Thing_2019_TV_series.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swamp_Thing_(2019_TV_series)"},{"title":"Swamp","blocks":[{"text":"A swamp is a forested wetland. Swamps are considered to be transition zones because both land and water play a role in creating this environment. Swamps vary in size and are located all around the world. The water of a swamp may be fresh water, brackish water, or seawater. Freshwater swamps form along large rivers or lakes where they are critically dependent upon rainwater and seasonal flooding to maintain natural water level fluctuations. Saltwater swamps are found along tropical and subtropical coastlines. Some swamps have hammocks, or dry-land protrusions, covered by aquatic vegetation, or vegetation that tolerates periodic inundation or soil saturation. The two main types of swamp are \"true\" or swamp forests and \"transitional\" or shrub swamps. In the boreal regions of Canada, the word swamp is colloquially used for what is more formally termed a bog, fen, or muskeg. Some of the world's largest swamps are found along major rivers such as the Amazon, the Mississippi, and the Congo."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Florida_freshwater_swamp_usgov_image.jpg/330px-Florida_freshwater_swamp_usgov_image.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swamp"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/59/Swthing01.jpg/250px-Swthing01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/59/Swthing01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/59/Swthing01.jpg/250px-Swthing01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cover of Swamp Thing #1 (October–November 1972), art by Bernie Wrightson","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASwthing01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/72/Swampthingmoore21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/72/Swampthingmoore21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Cover of The Saga of the Swamp Thing (vol. 2) #21 (February 1984), art by Tom Yeates","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASwampthingmoore21.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/78/SwampThingComicAd.jpg/250px-SwampThingComicAd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/78/SwampThingComicAd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/78/SwampThingComicAd.jpg/250px-SwampThingComicAd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A comic book ad for the 1990 TV series.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASwampThingComicAd.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/32/Swamp_Thing_%28Derek_Mears%29.jpg/250px-Swamp_Thing_%28Derek_Mears%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/32/Swamp_Thing_%28Derek_Mears%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/32/Swamp_Thing_%28Derek_Mears%29.jpg/250px-Swamp_Thing_%28Derek_Mears%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbna